Open Mic Host, played by Paul F. Tompkins.

11
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:15,000
Lil' JB, played by Troy Gentile.

12
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
Tenacious D in The Pick of Destiny is a 2006 American musical
fantasy comedy film about comedy rock duo Tenacious D.

13
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:33,000
Written, produced by and starring Tenacious D members Jack Black and Kyle Gass, it
is directed and co-written by musician and puppeteer Liam Lynch.

14
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:12,000
Despite being about an actual band, the film is a fictitious story about the band's origins, and their
journey to find a magical pick belonging to Satan that allows its users to become rock legends.

15
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
The film was released on November 22, 2006, and was a box office bomb.

16
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
The soundtrack, The Pick of Destiny, was also released in
2006 as the band's second studio album.

17
01:19:03,000 --> 01:19:09,000
Despite the mixed box office reception of the film at release,
it has since been considered a cult classic.

18
01:23:42,000 --> 01:23:48,000
The film explores themes of rock 'n' roll, guitar,
rock star, music competition, satan.

19
01:28:21,000 --> 01:28:27,000
The tone is lighthearted.
